"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jeff Bezos pledges $100 million to save endangered species]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135210311.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/jeff-bezos-commits-100-million-to-a-500-million-wildlife-alliance-targeting-31000-endangered-species-as-global-conservation-funding-falls-short/articleshow/135210311.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/jeff-bezos-commits-100-million-to-a-500-million-wildlife-alliance-targeting-31000-endangered-species-as-global-conservation-funding-falls-short/articleshow/135210311.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-01T01:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Tech Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135210409,imgsize-308836.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1874 Kansas City building saved from demolition, set to become restaurant and apartments]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135376766.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Kansas City, a historic gem originally at risk of being demolished is undergoing a transformation into a vibrant restaurant and apartment space. Developer Chris Sally acquired the Seiden's Furs building following a partial roof collapse. The renovation plans honor the building’s historical elements while modernizing its infrastructure. The new restaurant, Loretta Jean's, is set to welcome diners in autumn 2026, contributing to the preservation of Kansas City’s architectural heritage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kansas-city-building-dating-to-1874-faced-emergency-demolition-after-part-of-its-roof-collapsed-a-developer-stepped-in-and-the-former-fur-shop-is-now-being-turned-into-a-restaurant-and-apartments/articleshow/135376766.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kansas-city-building-dating-to-1874-faced-emergency-demolition-after-part-of-its-roof-collapsed-a-developer-stepped-in-and-the-former-fur-shop-is-now-being-turned-into-a-restaurant-and-apartments/articleshow/135376766.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-01T00:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135377896,imgsize-1482093.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rare 1928 Bentley worth seven figures found abandoned in British barn, awaiting authentication]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135377911.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a fascinating discovery, urban explorer Colin Smith found a 1928 Bentley 4.5 Litre Sports Tourer buried under layers of dust in an old barn. The car, featuring its untouched Vanden Plas bodywork, represents a significant relic, with only 148 produced. The next steps involve expert authentication and restoration to prepare it for sale, as auction records for similar models show varied estimates based on condition.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-british-explorer-filming-an-abandoned-barn-found-a-rare-1928-bentley-4-5-litre-sports-tourer-one-of-148-four-seat-vanden-plas-examples-it-could-be-worth-seven-figures-but-its-identity-remains-unverified/articleshow/135377911.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-british-explorer-filming-an-abandoned-barn-found-a-rare-1928-bentley-4-5-litre-sports-tourer-one-of-148-four-seat-vanden-plas-examples-it-could-be-worth-seven-figures-but-its-identity-remains-unverified/articleshow/135377911.cms]]></guid><pubDate>202